  "description": "<p>Queries in the SPO language do not seem to match typed literals correctly, regardless of triple store used (Mulgara,MPTStore)</p>\n\n<p>A query such as this:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>&lt;info:fedora/fedora-system:def/view#lastModifiedDate&gt; 2008-07-02T05:09:44.375Z^^&lt;<a href=\"http://fark.com\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fark.com</a>&gt;</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>will result in a positive match to a triple such as (note that object literal types don't match:<br/>\n&lt;info:fedora/test:123&gt; &lt;info:fedora/fedora-system:def/view#lastModifiedDate&gt; 2008-07-02T05:09:44.375Z^^&lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime</a>&gt;</p>\n\n<p>In addition, surrounding the typed literal value in quotes results in 500 error:<br/>\n'2008-07-02T05:09:44.375Z'^^&lt;<a href=\"http://fark.com\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fark.com</a>&gt;<br/>\n\"2008-07-02T05:09:44.375Z\"^^&lt;<a href=\"http://fark.com\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fark.com</a>&gt;</p>\n\n<p>SPOnge queries work as expected (but this language is not available with Mulgara)</p>",
